{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbouPvB3hi9n4JBKkD1h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I don't have a file-writing tool in this session, so here is the script for you to save as `print_groups.py` next to `inventory.ini`:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Print hosts from a static Ansible INI inventory, grouped by group name.\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\n\n\ndef parse_inventory(path):\n    groups = OrderedDict()\n    children = {}\n    current = \"ungrouped\"\n    section_type = \"hosts\"\n\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        for raw in fh:\n            line = raw.split(\"#\", 1)[0].split(\";\", 1)[0].strip()\n            if not line:\n                continue\n\n            if line.startswith(\"[\") and line.endswith(\"]\"):\n                name = line[1:-1].strip()\n                if \":\" in name:\n                    name, section_type = name.split(\":\", 1)\n                else:\n                    section_type = \"hosts\"\n                current = name\n                if section_type in (\"hosts\", \"children\"):\n                    groups.setdefault(current, [])\n                continue\n\n            if section_type == \"hosts\":\n                host = line.split()[0]  # drop inline vars like ansible_host=...\n                if host not in groups.setdefault(current, []):\n                    groups[current].append(host)\n            elif section_type == \"children\":\n                children.setdefault(current, []).append(line.split()[0])\n            # [group:vars] sections are ignored\n\n    return groups, children\n\n\ndef resolve(group, groups, children, seen=None):\n    \"\"\"Return the group's own hosts plus the hosts of its child groups.\"\"\"\n    seen = seen or set()\n    if group in seen:\n        return []\n    seen.add(group)\n    hosts = list(groups.get(group, []))\n    for child in children.get(group, []):\n        for h in resolve(child, groups, children, seen):\n            if h not in hosts:\n                hosts.append(h)\n    return hosts\n\n\ndef main():\n    path = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else \"inventory.ini\"\n    groups, children = parse_inventory(path)\n\n    for group in groups:\n        hosts = resolve(group, groups, children)\n        if group == \"ungrouped\" and not hosts:\n            continue\n        print(f\"{group}:\")\n        for host in hosts:\n            print(f\"  {host}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nRun it with:\n\n```\npython3 print_groups.py inventory.ini\n```\n\nI haven't run it, but when I trace it by hand against your current `inventory.ini`, it should print:\n\n```\nweb:\n  web01.example.com\n  web02.example.com\ndb:\n  db01.example.com\n```\n\nYour inventory is just two plain groups. The script also handles a few things you might add later:\n- **Variables on a host line** (`web01 ansible_host=10.0.0.1`): it keeps only the hostname.\n- **`[group:children]`**: a parent group lists the hosts of its child groups.\n- **`[group:vars]`**: these sections are skipped.\n- **Comments** starting with `#` or `;`: ignored.\n- **Hosts above the first header**: they go under `ungrouped`.\n\nIt does **not** expand host ranges like `web[01:10].example.com`. If you need that, or full Ansible behaviour, `ansible-inventory -i inventory.ini --graph` gives a similar tree using Ansible's own parser."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":191,"cache_read_input_tokens":12407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":191},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb042527-ca49-4241-b260-24f0286aa60e","uuid":"a2008676-08f5-4e9c-b9d9-473d5152530f","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:25:20.959Z","request_id":"req_011CgbouPgXvXAe93CJXSxvQ"}
